      "id": 1,
      "text": "Gabbs, Nevada began in December 1941 as a company town built for Basic Magnesium, Inc.'s war‑time magnesium production.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gabbs%2C_Nevada"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town takes its name from Gabbs Valley, itself named after paleontologist William Gabb who studied local fossils.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gabbs%2C_Nevada"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Gabbs' magnesium plant shut down in September 1944 after producing enough ore to meet wartime targets.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gabbs%2C_Nevada"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Gabbs officially incorporated on March 29, 1955, solidifying its status beyond a company town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gabbs%2C_Nevada"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Gabbs is known for hosting Nevada's largest tarantula migration each spring, drawing curious visitors.",
